  <object id="92" name="EP_Proto_5" type="Dialogue" x="1360" y="520">
   <properties>
    <property name="Dialogue Type" value="first"/>
    <property name="Next 1" type="object" value="103"/>
    <property name="Text 1" value="I see, that's quite the journey. If the previous Underking is already making a move, then this is serious. It looks like we'll need all the help we can get. After the Cybeast incident, we couldn't rely on only a few extraordinary NetBattlers. So the Officials approved a regulated initiative: the 'Legend' Program. This program was created by the NetBattler Officials to train regular battlers. We're allowing 'Echo' Navis to be mass produced. They're copies patterned after Legendary Navi feats, used by battlers to hone their skills. You probably already used a few 'Echo' Navis before. Thing is, 'Echo' Navis aren't supposed to drop NaviChips. How could they? They're just copies, it doesn't have the Navi's original programming. The fact that an 'Echo' Navi dropped this means some protocols are being ignored. Something deep is going on. The 'Legend' program is being overseen by the Officials, sure, but we don't directly produce the 'Echo' Navis. If the manufacturer is doing something shady, then we should've caught on immediately. The fact that SSS NetBattler Officials are being kept in the dark, and Serenade is already making a move, can only mean there could be corruption on the inside."/>
   </properties>
   <point/>
  </object>
